    "title": "Couple Paul Thomas Anderson and Maya Rudolph's Major Oscars 2026 Moments",
    "text": "Many celebrity couples were supporting each other on Oscar night. Paul Thomas Anderson had a big night as the writer and director of One Battle After Another. He has been in a relationship with Maya Rudolph since 2001.They're not married and have four children. Rudolph, 53, wasn't there only to support her partner, but she reunited with former cast members.Bridesmaid Cast ReunitesAnderson, 55, won an Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay and Directing. He said the action movie was inspired by his kids. The writer spoke about the meaning of the film in his acceptance speech.\"I wrote this movie for my kids, to say sorry for the housekeeping mess that we left in this world we’re handing off to them,\" he said. \"But also with the encouragement that they will be the generation that they will hopefully be the generation that brings us some common sense and decency.\"Related: Oscars 2026: Who Are the Surprise Guests in ‘Sinners’ Musical Performance?Rudolph later reunited with her Bridesmaids costars 15 years after the comedy's release. Rose Byrne, Kristen Wiig, Melissa McCarthy, and Ellie Kemper were on stage. \"Now, we are not good with numbers, but we figured out backstage that means we shot this movie in 1883,\" Wiig, 52 joke.Each actor pretended to read notes from people in the audience. They would then cut to the celebrity's reaction. \"Well, mine says, ‘First of all, you ladies look extremely beautiful tonight.’ Oh, that’s nice,\" Rudolph said. \"‘You’re all aging well. Signed, Stellan Skarsgård.'\"Related: How Long Have Oscar 2026 Winner Amy Madigan and Ed Harris Been Married?\"Oh, this one’s for me,\" Byrne said. \"‘Rose, can you please stop looking at me? The eye contact is too much. I’m thinking of leaving. I’m so uncomfortable. Sincerely, Leonardo DiCaprio.’ I apologize, I have been staring at you. I thought you were somebody else.\"One Battle After Another was nominated 13 times. It won the first Best Casting Academy Award. Sean Penn won his third Oscar for his performance, but wasn't there to accept his award.This story was originally published by Parade on Mar 16, 2026, where it first appeared in the Celebs section. Add Parade as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
